son cites Goldman’s global spending forecast as context; prior questions track hyperscaler spending rather than global AI spending.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k09\",\"coverage\":\"none\",\"prior\":[],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The cash-flow analysis cites “$25 billion of equity-investment commitments at July 26”; no prior question tracks that aggregate balance.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k10\",\"coverage\":\"none\",\"prior\":[],\"article\":\"news\",\"matter_is\":\"new\",\"why\":\"The report says MIIT “intends to approve” purchases of the RTX Pro 5500, which “was released this month.”\"}\n{\"id\":\"k11\",\"coverage\":\"same_matter\",\"prior\":[\"w1\"],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The stock overview says Nvidia offers to “cover up to 25% of the loss”; w1 tracks broader customer credit support.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k12\",\"coverage\":\"none\",\"prior\":[],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The analyst overview mentions “larger supply commitments” as a risk; no prior question tracks the total in Nvidia's annual report.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k13\",\"coverage\":\"none\",\"prior\":[],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The stock recommendation cites management's expected “moderate rise in prices”; prior questions do not track memory price changes.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k14\",\"coverage\":\"same_matter\",\"prior\":[\"v4\"],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The recommendation cites spending by the “big five” as context; v4 tracks the same year's spending for four hyperscalers.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k15\",\"coverage\":\"same_matter\",\"prior\":[\"w1\"],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The stock comparison recounts guarantees “signed in August”; w1 tracks the broader total of customer credit support and guarantees.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k16\",\"coverage\":\"same_matter\",\"prior\":[\"v64\"],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The comparison notes Nvidia “recently agreed to acquire Hugging Face”; v64 asks about an agreement, not completion.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k17\",\"coverage\":\"same_matter\",\"prior\":[\"v61\"],\"article\":\"news\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The article reports a new lawsuit and says Groq 3 LPX is “already in full production”; v61 follows its Nebius deployment.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k18\",\"coverage\":\"none\",\"prior\":[],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The GPU-access overview mentions the B200 spot price “has more than doubled since March”; no prior question tracks that price.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k19\",\"coverage\":\"same_matter\",\"prior\":[\"v20\",\"v21\"],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The stock comparison says Vera Rubin “has entered the full production stage”; v20 and v21 follow sampling and customer shipments.\"}\n{\"id\":\"k20\",\"coverage\":\"same_question\",\"prior\":[\"w2\"],\"article\":\"background\",\"matter_is\":\"standing\",\"why\":\"The stock comparison cites “$279 billion of supply and capacity commitments”; w2 already tracks their next annual-report total.\"}"}}
